          "The rise of social media has unfortunately amplified many health myths. Personal experiences, misleading videos, and unverified health advice often spread much faster than evidence-based medical information. A mother who develops a breast lump while breastfeeding may wrongly assume that the breast pump caused it, even though the lump may actually be due to a blocked duct, mastitis, or another benign condition. This confusion keeps the question “Can Breast Pump Cause Cancer?” circulating despite decades of research proving otherwise.",
