          "Another warning sign that should never be ignored is bloody nipple discharge , particularly if it occurs from one breast without squeezing the nipple. While infections or benign conditions can occasionally cause discharge, blood-stained discharge may sometimes indicate an underlying breast abnormality, including cancer. Any unexplained bloody discharge requires prompt medical assessment.",
