          "By now, we’ve established that the answer to “Can Breast Pump Cause Cancer?” is a clear no . Scientific research consistently shows that breast pumps do not increase the risk of breast cancer. However, using a breast pump correctly is essential to ensure comfort, maintain milk supply, and prevent common breastfeeding-related problems. As a Medical Oncologist, I often reassure mothers that while Can Breast Pump Cause Cancer is a myth, improper pumping techniques can lead to temporary discomfort that is easily preventable with the right approach.",
          "The first and perhaps most important step is to choose the correct flange size . The flange, also called the breast shield, is the part of the pump that fits over the nipple. A flange that is too small can compress the nipple, causing pain, friction, and poor milk flow. On the other hand, a flange that is too large may pull excessive breast tissue into the tunnel, resulting in discomfort and inefficient pumping. Most manufacturers offer multiple flange sizes, and selecting the correct fit can significantly improve both comfort and milk expression. Remember, discomfort caused by an ill-fitting flange does not mean Can Breast Pump Cause Cancer —it simply means the equipment needs adjustment.",
