          "One of the most frequently asked questions in my clinic is, “Is Blood Cancer Hereditary?” It is a concern that affects not only patients but also their parents, children, and siblings. When one family member is diagnosed with leukemia, lymphoma, or multiple myeloma, it is natural to wonder whether other relatives are also at risk. While family history can sometimes play a role, the reassuring fact is that most blood cancers are not hereditary .",
