          "After discussing “Is Blood Cancer Hereditary?” , the next question I usually hear from patients is, “If it isn’t hereditary, does that mean it isn’t genetic?” This is one of the biggest misconceptions surrounding blood cancers. The truth is that every blood cancer is genetic, but not every blood cancer is hereditary . Understanding this difference can help patients and their families avoid unnecessary fear while making informed decisions about their health.",
