          "Medical History",
          "The first step is taking a detailed medical history . I ask about symptoms such as persistent fever, unexplained weight loss, fatigue, night sweats, frequent infections, bone pain, or abnormal bleeding. Family history is also reviewed, especially if patients are concerned about “Is Blood Cancer Hereditary?” . Although inherited blood cancers are uncommon, a strong family history or known genetic syndrome may influence further investigations.",
